# --- Personal app data: never commit your own notes/attachments ---
# notes_data*.json covers notes_data.json itself plus the timestamped
# backups backup_notes_file()/_timestamped_backup() create next to it
# (notes_data_backup_<stamp>.json, notes_data_replaced_<stamp>.json) —
# those are just as much real user data as notes_data.json itself.
notes_data*.json
settings.json
trash.json
templates.json
attachments/
# Names the folder a source run keeps its notebook in, on this machine
# (core/paths.LOCATION_FILE): a path to one person's own folder.
notebook_location.txt

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- PyInstaller build artifacts ---
build/
dist/
# Auto-generated specs (from "pyinstaller script.py") are throwaway, but
# NoteOrganizer.spec is the hand-maintained build recipe this project
# actually ships with — see CLAUDE.md. Ignoring it meant build settings
# (e.g. the numpy exclusion) lived only on one machine and couldn't be
# reproduced from a fresh clone or in CI.
*.spec
!NoteOrganizer.spec

# --- The website (site/): what its build makes ---
# site/build.py writes the finished site into site/public/, staged in
# site/public.building/ first. That is what goes to Netlify, and it is made
# again from site/src/ and this repository whenever it is needed.
site/public/
site/public.building/

# --- Editor / OS cruft ---
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
# Claude Code's permission lists: machine-specific (absolute paths, this
# user's home directory) and not part of the product. This line is
# deliberate rather than decorative. `settings.json` further up has no
# leading slash, so it already matches `.claude/settings.json` at any
# depth — meaning anchoring that line to `/settings.json`, which is the
# correct fix for the app's own settings file, would silently make this
# one committable.
.claude/settings.json

# --- Runtime artifacts the app writes beside itself when run from source ---
# crash_log.txt is the app's own last-resort logger; the .tmp is a save
# that failed partway and is overwritten by the next successful save.
crash_log.txt
notes_data.json.tmp

# The single-instance lock: created beside the notebook on every launch
# (the repo root, when run from source) and kept while the app is open.
.notebook.lock

# --- QA scratch files (keep the tracked test plan, ignore working copies) ---
qa/__pycache__/
qa/*.json
# Excel's lock beside an open workbook (~$NoteOrganizer_TestPlan.xlsx):
# never part of the plan, and a `git add qa/` would otherwise take it.
~$*

# Icon comparison sheets and previews: artefacts of choosing a design,
# regenerated any time by `py tools/make_icon.py --sheet`. Only the two
# files the app actually ships are tracked.
assets/previews/
